method (it always comparing keys and track types) is to be used, I assume hashes should not be used in the first place.\r\n\r\nI think it would be comforting if we could check for collisions only once during hash generation and then increment the int as avoidance, but we should probably consider the performance cost of the collision check since it will likely require iterating over all hashes within the AnimationLibrary. It should probably be done only once after the animation loads and all tracks have finished generating their hashes, rather than during hash generation. Using something like a `hash_dirty` flag for deferred calls might be a preferable approach.\r\n\r\nOr, the approach would be to either discontinue hashing and instead compare pointers to a single concatenated StringName formed by concatenating the path and track_cache type with special characters, or adopt a 256-bit hash with compromising on the astronomical collision probability.","created_at":"2025-09-12T07:09:50Z","updated_at":"2025-09-12T07:35:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110439#discussion_r2343224973","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110439","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2343224973"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110439#discussion_r2343224973"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110439"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2343224973/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":1146,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":118,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2343349950","pull_request_review_id":3215281726,"id